{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1530279-how-does-monotheism-work-in-scion","id":1530279,"title":"How does Monotheism work in Scion?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-08T08:55:35-08:00","id":1530279,"title":"How does Monotheism work in Scion?","content":"How does it exist in the first place, and how mainstream is it? Like the book seem to indicate that Monotheism are bigger than cult, but their isn't really a Scion for Monotheism that I can find.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","user":"Yumlum","date":". 02-08-2024, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T09:39:13-08:00","id":1530284,"title":"","content":"It depends on where you turn the dial for the secrecy of scions and their deeds in the World.<br /> <br /> The default assumption is that scions and the gods are publically known enough that monotheism doesn't work. <i>Henotheism,</i> however, still does: acknowledging the existence of multiple gods, but devoting yourself to the worship of only one or a few. The existence of the pantheons disproves the idea that the God of the Abrahamic faiths is the only god, but it doesn't disprove that he exists. One can imagine arguments that a supreme god has a more subtle touch on the World than the pantheonic divinities, who need to act more directly, personally or through scions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T11:13:37-08:00","id":1530292,"title":"","content":"Also, Primordials are in the game to enable this sort of thing. There are numerous Pantheons than have one god who is above all the rest \u2014 not just first among equals, but a being that's on a whole other level from the others \u2014 and that model can be used to describe a Monotheistic deity. <br /> <br /> There's no \u201cGod of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob\u201d in the game because it's a subject that's nearly impossible to handle respectfully; but there are several fan-made \u201cAbrahamic Pantheons\u201d that have been posted on these forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T13:01:37-08:00","id":1530396,"title":"","content":"What about Henotheism. Henotheism is were you worship one god but you don't necessarily denigrate the others or deny their existence. Most Henotheists say this is my/our god. You have your god/s and that's what you want. This is what we have and follow. Christianity might simply say, those are other gods, but our God is what we want/follow/celebrate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T14:45:36-08:00","id":1530404,"title":"","content":"That's not really an issue, as each mythology need only be internally consistent; it doesn't need to be consistent with other mythologies. For instance, the Hindu mythology defines the Zoroastrian gods as demons, and vice versa; but that's okay, because the Zoroastrian gods are defined by Zoroastrian mythology, not Hindu mythology, and vice versa. <br /> <br /> So it's entirely possible for an Abrahamic mythology to be internally Monotheistic (that is, the mythology only defines one God, with other supernatural entities such as angels being defined as supernatural denizens) and thus not be a problem. They're not likely to have friendly relations with other* Pantheons; but they don't have to in order to be a valid Pantheon. <br /> <br /> To me, the real issue is whether the Jewish, Christian, and Islamic mythologies can reasonably be merged into one whole being respectful to each. Plus there's the issue of the various \u201cspinoffs\u201d such as the Samaritans, the Mormons and Jehovah's Witnesses, and the various internal divisions within each, and whether or not those differences can be rectified in a way that's respectful to each. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bIt's a potential quagmire; and I cannot fault Onyx Path for choosing to stay out of it. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">* I'm using the term \u201cPantheon\u201d loosely here, to refer to the mythological structure without reference to how many gods are part of it. Technically, they'd be \u201cMonotheons\u201d; but saying \u201cMonotheons and Pantheons\u201d is clunky.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T12:14:29-08:00","id":1530465,"title":"","content":"First, stop referring to Christianity (or Abrahamic religions in general) only as \u201cmonotheism.\u201d Candomble and Zoroastrianism are also monotheistic and canonical in Scion. Regarding your question, all mythologies coexist; that includes the Bible and other holy books, even if they contradict each other. In Scion 1E, they almost imply that YHVH is Aten and that the biblical events are misinterpreted attempts to attack humans (fortunately, this is no longer the case). The most popular headcanon is that YHVH is a primordial who stands above all the chaos of the events of Scion, acting in more subtle ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1530279-how-does-monotheism-work-in-scion?p=1530404#post1530404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not really an issue, as each mythology need only be internally consistent; it doesn't need to be consistent with other mythologies. For instance, the Hindu mythology defines the Zoroastrian gods as demons, and vice versa; but that's okay, because the Zoroastrian gods are defined by Zoroastrian mythology, not Hindu mythology, and vice versa.<br /> <br /> So it's entirely possible for an Abrahamic mythology to be internally Monotheistic (that is, the mythology only defines one God, with other supernatural entities such as angels being defined as supernatural denizens) and thus not be a problem. They're not likely to have friendly relations with other* Pantheons; but they don't have to in order to be a valid Pantheon.<br /> <br /> To me, the real issue is whether the Jewish, Christian, and Islamic mythologies can reasonably be merged into one whole being respectful to each. Plus there's the issue of the various \u201cspinoffs\u201d such as the Samaritans, the Mormons and Jehovah's Witnesses, and the various internal divisions within each, and whether or not those differences can be rectified in a way that's respectful to each.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's a potential quagmire; and I cannot fault Onyx Path for choosing to stay out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That Hinduism thing you mentioned is a error, there are no demonic equivalents in Hinduism to the Persian gods.<br /> Rather it is the other way around, some Zoroastrian Daevas have names derived from Hindu gods, Indar for example\u200b<br /> <br /> Regarding the relationship of the &quot;Abrahamic pantheon&quot; with others, yes, it would be mostly negative; The only pantheons that I think would be more neutral/positive with them would be Theoi (For their cultural connection with Catholicism), Tuatha D\u00e9 Danann (For being descendants of Noah) and Apus (For the enriched integration of the Tahuantinsuyo to the Spanish empire)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28200,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28200-plebsparks","user":"PlebSparks","date":". 02-10-2024, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28200-plebsparks","name":"PlebSparks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28200_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T16:52:03-08:00","id":1530501,"title":"","content":"IIRC in 1e the mythic and supernatural was much more hidden, real world religions were dominant in the mundane world, and the exact question of 'how do these relate to the mythic' was a bit up in the air. There was a primordial controlling part of... I want to say the Catholic Church but I'm not certain but a) it had grown beyond his control and b) wasn't even his idea in the first plce. It also has a homebrew Caananite pantheon, but I believe it sidesteps stuff by omitting the specific god this would be Fatebinding.<br /> <br /> As people have covered 2e presumes that the mythic is more open. Thus monotheism can only really survive by the practitioners making a distinction between 'gods' and 'God(s)'c, but as others have mentioned there are alternatives available. It's possible that YHVH is just a god like any other, in a pantheon that hasn't been covered and may never be, and nobody in-setting cares enough to correct the 'this dude is the greatest god' thing. That would be how I'd run it if players insisted on having an answer (and no you cannot play a scion of that pantheon, I don't know enough to homebrew ti and YHVH isn't taking calls).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T17:18:54-08:00","id":1530503,"title":"","content":"I've seen the game refer to Church, but is those Church of the Pantheon or for the Monothestic religion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T20:09:48-08:00","id":1530527,"title":"","content":"\u201c<i>the</i> Monotheistic religion\u201d, as if there's only one of those? <br /> <br /> <b>Mysteries of the World</b> introduces a series of Myth Levels which you can use to specify the overall approach that you want your games to take. It gives you four categories (Genre, Theocentrism, Titanomachy, and Evidence) that can be rated at one of five levels (Iron, Heroic, Bronze, Silver, and Gold). Theocentrism in particular specifically \u201ccontemplates the role of monotheistic religions in humanity's body of myth.\u201d Under that section, you get this: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>page 12</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Monotheism/Henotheism:</b> Monotheism by its nature does not recognize the divinity of any deities other than its own, but The World is already consistently contradictory, and monotheism is just another cosmological truth that shares space with every other truth. In the default World, henotheism is much more common, and even monotheistic religions have space for God-like entities that can form pantheons around the primary God. A series where monotheism is the dominant cosmology, regardless of the Theocentrism level, changes the World in different ways than if a polytheistic pantheon is dominant.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Theocentrism axis is about how many or how few different Pantheons feature in your version of the World.<br /> <br /> At Iron level, only one is featured: all of the protagonists are scions of that one Pantheon, and they don't interact with unadulterated version of any other Pantheon. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When monotheism is the focus, the reigning \u201cpantheon\u201d has only one <i>true</i> God, and everything supernatural with which the characters interact obeys the rules of that God's cosmology. If other \u201cGods\u201d exist in game terms, as beings the character can be the Scions of, they are demons and devils if they oppose the deity, or angels and saints if they align with it. </div> </div> </div>Heroic Theocentrism \u201cstill focuses on one or several dominant pantheons, but other mythologies' Gods, Scions, and associated creatures of Legend make appearances.\u201d <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Heroic monotheism includes peripheral myths as part of its core cosmology by default, such as the ifrit of Islam and the Abrahamic Nephilim\u2026 Syncretism is the name of the game when it comes to the dominant religion interacting with others </div> </div> </div>Bronze Theocentrism \u201cstill focuses mainly on the chosen mythologies, but other pantheons' agents needle frequently and independently in events.\u201d <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bronze-level monotheism doesn't have such a right hold on the story. While monotheistic tenets and archetypes remain dominant, polytheistic pantheons are known to be their own entities. </div> </div> </div>In Silver Theocentrism, \u201cthe story includes all pantheons at relatively equal strength and prominence, but one or a few get preferential treatment in the World in ways that create interesting story hooks.\u201d <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Monotheism goes full henotheism at the Silver level, as the more open inclusion of other pantheons makes it impossible for most of The World to follow monotheistic dogma too the letter. </div> </div> </div>Finally: in Gold Theocentrism (the default setting), \u201cevery myth is 100% true, and no pantheon claims dominance over the others except locally. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Monotheism in a Gold Theocentrism chronicle works just the same, its religions' cosmologies existing alongside all the other true myths, with nothing that makes them stand above other pantheons other than the breadth of their following. </div> </div> </div>Note that the first edition of the game included a group known as the Order of the Divine Glory. This group had its foundations in ancient Egypt, during a time when the Pharaoh introduced monotheism to the World for the first time, and concocting a plan to Fatebind a God (Ra) to empower him and his empire alone. He failed; but when the Hebrew slaves left Egypt, they took his techniques with them; and centuries later, under King Hezekiah, they put them into practice with much more success. Though eventually, their efforts were also crushed. The third time was the charm, though, as Christianity eventually sprung up from the remains of the Judaic experiment. <br /> <br /> The Order of the Divine Glory was presented as tied not just to Christianity, but also to Judaism, Zoroastrian faiths, Islam, and monotheistic religions in general. It was created to present a vision of monotheism in a setting where polytheistic beliefs were treated as more fundamentally true, though; and it shows. If the Order of the Divine Glory exists in 2e, it's likely to be very different: to the extent that its mythology was fabricated, it's no different than how <i>all</i> mythologies in <b>Scion</b> were originally fabrications, until they weren't. <br /> <br /> Again, my main objection to an Order of Divine Glory in <b>Scion</b> 2e isn't how it interacts with non-monotheistic pantheons, but rather how it tries to lump all monotheistic mythologies together. That right there is the single biggest difficulty in introducing monotheistic faiths into the setting in a way that's respectful of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}